# Monday policy: five channel recommendations (our opinion), each pinned to a moment of the night. Derived from AWS's summary; not AWS's instructions.
...@_style
(** -> **)[*].style: {stroke: "#5B7CBA"; font-color: "#8A9EC0"; stroke-width: 2}
direction: down
p1: "1 · 11:48 PM stale check\nmake the write conditional on the applied generation,\nchecked by the receiver in the same operation (fencing token);\nif it can't check → single writer\ndoes NOT solve: a newer plan that is wrong" {class: svc}
p2: "2 · 11:48 PM cleanup\nfloor under destructive automation:\nnever delete what's active; never publish 0 targets\n(or far below last size) without a human\ndoes NOT solve: a plan that is bad but not empty" {class: svc}
p3: "3 · 12:38 AM identification\nsynthetic DNS check: page on 0 answers\nor a sudden drop in answer count; make it the page that names the cause\ndoes NOT solve: the fix; it detects, it doesn't contain" {class: svc}
p4: "4 · 6:45–9:36 AM capacity removed\ncap removals per interval + tested failover kill switch;\nfreeze what removes/replaces healthy instances; leave scale-out on\ndoes NOT solve: truly dead instances; it adds no capacity" {class: svc}
p5: "5 · 2:25–5:28 AM dependency returns\ndrill fleet-wide re-establishment vs timeout;\ndrop expired work; write the recovery runbook\ndoes NOT solve: the outage itself; it decides how you come back" {class: svc}
p1 -> p2 -> p3 -> p4 -> p5
foot: "Channel recommendations (our opinion), based on AWS's summary (aws.amazon.com/message/101925)" {class: note}
